<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
  <meta name="description" content="Explore this fortnight's curated Stockholm arts, music, and cultural events by date.">
  <title>Event Calendar · The Stockholm Guide · {{ data.date_range }}</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="./assets/stockholm-guide-favicon.svg">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f2f0eb">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./calendar.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="masthead-top">
        <a class="brand" href="./calendar.html" aria-label="Stockholm Guide calendar home">The<br>Stockholm<br>Guide</a>
        <div class="descriptor">A CURATED GUIDE TO<br>CULTURE, ART AND<br>IDEAS IN STOCKHOLM</div>
      </div>
      <div class="edition"><span>THE EVENT CALENDAR</span><span>{{ data.date_range }}</span><span>ISSUE #{{ data.issue_number }}</span></div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="introduction" aria-labelledby="main-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE BY DATE</p>
          <h1 id="main-heading">Good things are<br><em>happening.</em></h1>
          <p class="dek">Verified discoveries from all reviewed sources, including events that didn't fit in the email, arranged around your calendar. Choose a date, discover an event, then check the organizer for final details.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="count">{{ data.event_count }} CURATED EXPERIENCES<br><span>{{ data.date_range }}</span></p>
      </section>

      <section class="calendar-shell" aria-label="Events calendar">
        <div class="toolbar">
          <div class="view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Calendar display">
            <button type="button" data-view="calendar" aria-pressed="true" class="switch active">Calendar</button>
            <button type="button" data-view="list" aria-pressed="false" class="switch">All events</button>
          </div>
          <label class="search-label"><span class="sr-only">Search events</span>
            <input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search events or venues" autocomplete="off">
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="subscription-bar" aria-label="Calendar subscription">
          <div class="subscription-copy">
            <strong>Keep the good things coming.</strong>
            <span>Subscribe to the published event feed. It refreshes when a new issue is released.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="subscription-actions">
            <a class="subscribe-primary" href="{{ data.webcal_url }}">Subscribe to calendar</a>
            <button type="button" id="copy-subscription-url" class="subscription-control">Copy feed URL</button>
            <a class="subscription-control" href="{{ data.download_feed_url }}" download="stockholm-guide.ics">Download current .ics</a>
          </div>
          <p class="subscription-hint">Apple Calendar / Outlook: Subscribe. Google Calendar (desktop): Add calendar → From URL, then paste the feed link. Refresh timing is controlled by your calendar app. Only dated sessions and verified closing reminders are included.</p>
          <p class="copy-feedback" id="copy-subscription-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="filter-bar" id="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter events">
          <button type="button" class="filter active" aria-pressed="true" data-filter="all">All</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="top3">Top picks</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="new_discoveries">New discoveries</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="calendar_only_events">More verified events</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="worth_reconsidering">Reconsider</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="last_chance">Last chance</button>
        </div>

        <div class="calendar-panel">
          <div id="fullcalendar" aria-label="Interactive month and list calendar"></div>
          <div id="calendar-unavailable" class="unavailable-calendar" hidden>Calendar display is temporarily unavailable. The individual event listings below remain accessible.</div>
          <div class="day-details" aria-live="polite">
            <div class="section-band"><span class="section-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>EVENTS ON THIS DATE</span></div>
            <div class="day-title"><h3 id="day-heading">Select a date</h3><span id="day-count"></span></div>
            <div id="day-events" class="event-list"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <section class="flexible-section" aria-labelledby="flexible-title">
          <div class="flexible-head">
            <div class="section-band"><span class="section-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>VISIT WHEN IT SUITS</span></div>
            <h2 id="flexible-title">Ongoing &amp; flexible dates</h2>
            <p>Exhibitions and experiences without a confirmed single session time. A final-day pin is a closing reminder, not an invitation to arrive at that hour.</p>
          </div>
          <div id="flexible-events" class="event-list"></div>
        </section>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer><span>THE STOCKHOLM GUIDE · INDEPENDENTLY CURATED</span><span>Dates and tickets may change. Always confirm with the organizer. Times in Stockholm (CET/CEST).</span></footer>
  </div>
  <script id="calendar-data" type="application/json">{{ json_blob | safe }}</script>
  <!-- FullCalendar Standard v6 (MIT); pinned CDN build includes dayGrid, list, interaction and CSS. -->
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/fullcalendar@6.1.22/index.global.min.js" defer></script>
  <script src="./calendar.js" defer></script>
  <noscript><section class="noscript"><h2>Events in this issue</h2><p>Enable JavaScript for the interactive calendar. Organizer links remain available below.</p>
  {% for event in data.events %}<article><strong>{{ event.title }}</strong><p>{{ event.dates }} · {{ event.venue }}</p><a href="{{ event.url }}">Official event page</a></article>{% endfor %}</section></noscript>
</body>
</html>
